$\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.$"} :step/id #uuid "a7ad5297-15e9-5030-bffe-fb54ed0eec36" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411463}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411467 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162719 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15485fac-790e-5582-90f5-2eb0336ce86a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ \\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411431} {:answer/id #uuid "51d9a677-8641-50b7-bf65-1ab6b97a0b4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ \\sqrt{11}\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{11} \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411436} {:answer/id #uuid "783c1108-45c5-5c61-b1de-135da5ea10e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411440} {:answer/id #uuid "96370f14-3c4b-563e-82b2-3cc6d00f55b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411444} {:answer/id #uuid "c141d751-a196-5cd6-b4cd-6bb466dd2ba0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411449}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411444} :answer-field/id #uuid "de22cbdd-1887-52e7-a256-745226952983" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411459}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "611baa25-d6cc-5c6f-9064-69e0865e9f0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-97986" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$ and the quadratic curve ${x}^{T}\\,Ax=2.$ Given that $A$ has eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=5$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=0,$ find the principal axes of the curve." :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is symmetric. \nThe principal axes of the curve \n\n$$\n{x}^{T}\\,Ax=2\n$$\n\nare the vectors that give an orthonormal eigenvector basis for $A.$ Let's now find these eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-5I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}-5\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-5I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ Dividing ${v}_{1}$ by its norm $‖{v}_{1}‖=\\sqrt{5},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-0I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}-0\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-0I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Dividing ${v}_{2}$ by its norm $‖{v}_{2}‖=\\sqrt{5},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the principal axes of our curve are\n\n$\\,$ $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$"} :step/id #uuid "c358e7c3-78df-5477-a368-888654cd7c35"}] :activity/title "Reducing a Quadratic Curve to Its Principal Axes" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review}